Naturally I just figured out how to copy text from a DOS box -
if you're playing with tiles (which I do), you have to switch to
ASCII mode.  Which I knew 2 years ago, but forgot.  Oh well.

Stuff I forgot to mention in the original post, for those who
care:

The MOST annoying thing in the whole game was teleportitis - I
didn't have it.  I ate a (hostile) tengu fairly early on, taking a gamble,
but I had a magic lamp at that point and figured it was worth it.
It was - I got teleport control.  I thought this was great - now I
could get teleportitis and not have to worry about using up a ring 
slot.  However, I couldn't get it for love (nymphs) or money (leprechauns),
despite mugging every one of them I saw (not knightly behavior, I know...).

I could have wished for a ring of teleport, but it really didn't seem
worth the slot.  I could also have wished for nymph tins, or something,
but I figured I had gotten that far without it, I would just continue.
I did use scrolls to teleport on the way back out of Gehennom on levels
where the stairs were really far apart, and I used level teleport traps
to go back to the Mines entrance a few times earlier in the game.

I would actually have said that not getting any gift other than Snickersnee
was more annoying than this (since I spent so much time sacrificing),
but it is nice to ascend a knight using Excalibur.  I'm still annoyed
at myself for losing a prior knight who had both Grayswandir and Stormbringer,
though (polyed into an umber hulk by a trap, forgot they had a bite attack).

Also, I did get into trouble once after getting rid of the master lich -
several monsters in succession managed to pick up a cockatrice corpse
and whack me with it in the Castle courtyard before I took care of it.
As I have a lizard corpse out at all times, not that big a deal, but
it gave me a bad moment or two.  After that I would say I was never close
to being in trouble until Astral - I was never seriously in trouble there,
but I did drop below 100 HP once (from a priest pounding me), and drank
a PoEH.


Special knight abilities:

#ride - useful in the early game, I didn't feel any need for it
after my horse got killed.  If I had found a scroll of taming I
would have tried taming a dragon and riding it, but that would be
more for style than anything.

#jump - I used this a handful of times.  I could have used it more
if I remembered about it - it would have been easier to use it to 
cross the moats inside Gehennom than swapping rings all the time,
for example, but it just didn't occur to me.  In theory I could
probably have crossed Medusa and Juiblex by jumping as well, but
I really didn't have the patience for that (for Medusa I would have
if I had no other way, of course, but I had at least two methods
by the time I finished the Quest).

#turn undead - I used this more with earlier knights, it seemed
problematic in that you were unable to move for several turns
afterwards, so any undead that resist it can pound on you. At higher
levels it is probably more effective, but at higher levels I really
didn't need it.  Would it actually be effective in, say, the Sanctum
graveyard?

